exports[`chunkMarkdown on the fixture notes > chunks programming.md the same way every time 1`] = `
[
  {
    "contentHash": "c83536287bbde9018a50f80d3649951f220bcb557800801bd496ef4f8be5d179",
    "heading": "Closures in JavaScript",
    "text": "A closure is a function together with the variables it captured from the scope where it was created. The function keeps access to those variables even after the outer function has returned.

\`\`\`js
function counter() {
  let count = 0;

  return () => ++count;
}
\`\`\`

Each call to \`counter()\` creates a new \`count\`, so two counters never share state. This is how modules hid private variables before JavaScript had classes and private fields.",
    "words": 74,
  },
]
`;
